---
import Base from "~/layouts/Base.astro";
import CodeBlock from "~/components/CodeBlock.astro";
import { CERT_IDENTITY_REGEXP, CERT_OIDC_ISSUER, loadEnrichedImages } from "~/lib/images";

const images = await loadEnrichedImages();
const sample =
  images.find((i) => i.featured)?.latest.artifacts.find((a) => a.fileUrl) ??
  images.flatMap((i) => i.latest.artifacts).find((a) => a.fileUrl);
const file = sample?.filename ?? "image.qcow2";
const fileUrl = sample?.fileUrl ?? "https://images.openimages.cloud/<os>/<version>/<file>";
const dir = fileUrl.slice(0, fileUrl.lastIndexOf("/") + 1);
const manifestName = sample?.manifestUrl.split("/").pop() ?? "MANIFEST.json";

const download = `curl -fLO ${fileUrl}
curl -fLO ${fileUrl}.bundle
curl -fLO ${dir}${manifestName}`;

const cosign = `cosign verify-blob ${file} \\
  --bundle ${file}.bundle --new-bundle-format \\
  --certificate-identity-regexp '${CERT_IDENTITY_REGEXP}' \\
  --certificate-oidc-issuer ${CERT_OIDC_ISSUER}`;

const checksum = `curl -fsSL ${fileUrl}.sha256 | sha256sum -c -`;

const inspect = `jq '{version, sha256, built_at, commit, build_url, builder}' ${manifestName}`;

const toc = [
  { id: "why", label: "What a signature proves" },
  { id: "install", label: "1. Install cosign" },
  { id: "download", label: "2. Download" },
  { id: "verify", label: "3. Verify the signature" },
  { id: "provenance", label: "4. Inspect provenance" },
  { id: "checksums", label: "Checksums only" },
];
---

<Base
  title="Verify an image"
  description="How to verify an Open Image Cloud image with cosign keyless signatures, checksums and the provenance manifest."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6 sm:py-20">
    <p class="eyebrow">Guide</p>
    <h1 class="text-ink mt-3 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Verify an image</h1>
    <p class="text-ink-muted mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed">
      Check that a file was built by our public CI and has not been altered since, before you boot
      it. It takes one command and no key management.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-12 grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[13rem_minmax(0,1fr)]">
      <nav aria-label="On this page" class="hidden lg:block">
        <ul class="sticky top-24 space-y-2 text-sm">
          {toc.map((t) => (
            <li>
              <a href={`#${t.id}`} class="text-ink-muted hover:text-ink">
                {t.label}
              </a>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </nav>

      <div class="min-w-0 max-w-3xl">
        <section id="why">
          <h2 class="text-ink text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">What a signature proves</h2>
          <p class="text-ink-muted mt-3 leading-relaxed">
            Images are signed with{" "}
            <a class="link" href="https://docs.sigstore.dev/">
              Sigstore
            </a>
            cosign in keyless mode. At build time GitHub Actions issues a short-lived OIDC identity
            for the exact workflow that runs; Sigstore's certificate authority binds the signature
            to that identity and records it in the public Rekor transparency log.
          </p>
          <ul class="text-ink-muted mt-4 space-y-2 leading-relaxed">
            <li class="flex gap-3">
              <span class="text-ok" aria-hidden="true">
                ✓
              </span>
              The file is byte-for-byte what our build produced.
            </li>
            <li class="flex gap-3">
              <span class="text-ok" aria-hidden="true">
                ✓
              </span>
              It was produced by one of the reusable build workflows in
              <a class="link" href="https://github.com/open-img-cloud/.github">
                open-img-cloud/.github
              </a>
              , not by a person or another repository.
            </li>
            <li class="flex gap-3">
              <span class="text-ok" aria-hidden="true">
                ✓
              </span>
              The signing event is publicly logged, so it cannot be issued silently.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="install" class="mt-14">
          <h2 class="text-ink text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">1. Install cosign</h2>
          <p class="text-ink-muted mt-3 leading-relaxed">
            Any recent cosign 2.x or 3.x release works. See the
            <a class="link" href="https://docs.sigstore.dev/cosign/system_config/installation/">
              installation guide
            </a>
            , or use a package manager:
          </p>
          <CodeBlock code="brew install cosign" label="Homebrew (macOS, Linux)" />
        </section>

        <section id="download" class="mt-14">
          <h2 class="text-ink text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">2. Download</h2>
          <p class="text-ink-muted mt-3 leading-relaxed">
            Fetch the image, its signature bundle and its manifest. They sit side by side under the
            same versioned path. Example with {file}:
          </p>
          <CodeBlock code={download} />
        </section>

        <section id="verify" class="mt-14">
          <h2 class="text-ink text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">3. Verify the signature</h2>
          <CodeBlock code={cosign} />
          <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">
            The output must be <code class="text-ok font-mono">Verified OK</code>. The identity
            pattern matches our three build workflows (libguestfs, diskimage-builder and Nix) on the{" "}
            <code class="font-mono text-sm">open-img-cloud/.github</code> repository: a signature
            from anywhere else is rejected.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="provenance" class="mt-14">
          <h2 class="text-ink text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">4. Inspect provenance</h2>
          <p class="text-ink-muted mt-3 leading-relaxed">
            The manifest records what was built, from which commit, by which CI run and with which
            builder container digest. Open the CI run to read the full build log.
          </p>
          <CodeBlock code={inspect} />
        </section>

        <section id="checksums" class="mt-14">
          <h2 class="text-ink text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Checksums only</h2>
          <p class="text-ink-muted mt-3 leading-relaxed">
            Without cosign you can still detect a corrupted download. Checksums alone don't prove
            who built the file, so prefer the signature when you can.
          </p>
          <CodeBlock code={checksum} />
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
